  "note": "Unchanged full measured source-index geometry splits, not independent accuracy ground truth. Full-input production 2.5D TIN with recorded XY duplicates/edge rejection; no voxel thinning, new coordinates or input resampling. Archived pre-change production worker supplies exact f32 distance, f64 summary and scalar PLY oracles; its first C2M output is excluded. Current fresh and cached controls use separate prewarmed contexts, identical TIN/input geometry and alternating execution order. Fresh rebuilds/copies the complete mesh for each original query slice. Cached owns immutable mesh/BVH on fewer resident workers under a 512 MiB aggregate reservation budget, and sends only queries on repeated calls. Both keep the original logical query slices and reset Morton order/warm guesses per slice, preserving signed/tie semantics; timings here are unsigned. Worker count reduction is part of the bounded cache policy, not an isolated same-concurrency cache effect. The current fresh constructor also uses exact-capacity triangle order storage instead of retaining centroid-vector capacity. Both contexts coexist during timing; idle cached BVHs remain resident during the fresh control. Whole RPC includes copies/transfers, query ordering/search, joining, summaries and returned arrays. Meshing/loading, pool startup, first observations, five warm-up rounds, bit/summary/export parity and cleanup excluded. Timed cached fallback/non-reuse or layout/budget mismatch fails. Retained bytes include source mesh and BVH vector capacities, not temporary query arrays, allocator/driver overhead or process/peak memory. Actual capacities checked against reservations; overlap reservations share the budget. Artifacts, relevant source, input/source/manifest and script hashes checked before/after. No builds/tests/scans alongside timing; clocks, power, other applications, scheduling and GC uncontrolled. No GPU model identifiers recorded."
